+Every mutation except `init` takes `--op <id>` and `--expect-seq <n>` (not needed with `--dry-run`); `init` takes only an optional `--op`. An identical request in the same phase and round under a new op id returns the committed result (`replayed: true`). Output is one JSON object on stdout: `{ok, seq, phase, review, fix_cycles, counts, loop_decision, delivery_outcome, next_action, ...}` for every subcommand but `verdict`, which prints `{verdict, loop_decision, delivery_outcome, U, review, phase}`; a refusal prints `{error, detail, next_action}`. Besides the codes in the table, every mutation can be refused `E-NO-LEDGER`, `E-TAMPERED`, `E-LOCKED`, `E-STALE-SEQ`, `E-OP-CONFLICT` or `E-USAGE` (a `--dry-run` call takes no lock and checks no sequence).
 
